Ladybird wraps the contents of a button in an anonymous button content
box only when the button’s display is neither flex nor grid, and treats
only that box as the content box.

Blink’s HTMLButtonElement::CreateLayoutObject() gives a flex or grid
button an ordinary layout object, and other buttons a LayoutBlockFlow.
Gecko’s nsCSSFrameConstructor::FindHTMLButtonData() lets a flex, grid
or flow-root button keep its display, and forces other buttons into a
block. And WebKit’s RenderButton holds the contents of every button in
an anonymous inner block, its m_inner.
